Template: dogecoin-core-pro/install-role
Type: select
Choices: Client - desktop wallet (ImGui), Server - headless operator (TUI + systemd), Hybrid - both UIs, one dogecoind
Choices-C: client, server, hybrid
Default: client
Description: How are you installing Dogecoin Core Pro?
 One dogecoind is installed in every case. The UIs share it; never run two nodes.
 .
 Client: desktop wallet. You start the GUI; it starts the node if needed.
 Datadir is the installing user's ~/.dogecoin. No systemd unit.
 .
 Server: headless operator (replaces dogecoin-gpenode). systemd unit
 dogecoin-core-pro, datadir /var/lib/dogecoin-core-pro.
 .
 Hybrid: both UIs, still one systemd dogecoind. Run dogecoin-core-pro
 and pick Desktop GUI or Operator TUI.
 .
 Reconfigure later with: sudo dpkg-reconfigure dogecoin-core-pro
 Noninteractive: debconf-set-selections (see /usr/share/doc/dogecoin-core-pro).
